pe' and 'int'\n```\n\nTrack down why this happens and fix it so the program runs cleanly. When it\nworks, `python3 main.py` should print exactly:\n\n```\nTotal: 5.0\n```\n\nDone when `python3 main.py` exits successfully and prints that line.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170212 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/963a926db24ea70f6002cde66d0ff858de06fae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: task]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe crash is fixed: `python3 main.py` now prints `Total: 5.0` and exits with code 0.\n\n- **Where `rate` became None (first subagent call):** `app/pricing.py:8`, which returns `SETTINGS.get(\"rate\")`. `.get` gives back `None` when a key doesn't exist instead of raising an error. That `None` reached `app/report.py:9` and caused the `TypeError`.\n- **Which settings key was missing (second call, same subagent session `ses_eb288ae8dffeLEn6CDE6Jczz0A`):** `\"rate\"`. Line 2 of `settings.json` had the typo `\"rat\": 0.5` instead.\n- **Fix:** I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"rate\"` in `settings.json:2`.\n\nThe subagent also suggested an optional change: using `SETTINGS[\"rate\"]` in `pricing.py` would make a missing key fail right away with a clear error. I didn't make that change; the typo fix alone is enough.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requ